0000:                   * DIR Edition #8 - Released Mar. 12/2000
0000:                   * Added the '-c' option, which stands for case insensitive. This means that
0000:                   *  wildcard filename matches do not care as to whether the filenames are
0000:                   * upper or lowercase, when compared to the wildcard filename search you
0000:                   * specified. There still are some quirks to using the '*' wildcard in some
0000:                   * cases... I am still tracking down why that is happening.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * DIR Edition #7 - Released Jan. 16/2000
0000:                   *
0000:                   * This is a new version of the DIR command, based on the version Alan Dekok
0000:                   *  did with wildcarding. It fixes the year to work with modern clock drivers,
0000:                   *  allowing from 1900-2155. It also fixes the help message, and changes the
0000:                   * edition # to 7. It should work with all version of OS9/NitrOS9/PowerBoost.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * -Curtis-
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edition #7: (L. Curtis Boyle)
0000:                   * 2000/01/15: Fixed help message bug.
0000:                   * 2000/01/16: Fixed year output to handle 1900-2155
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edition #8 (Curtis)
0000:                   * 2000/03/11  Fixed Bad Filename error
0000:                   * 2000/03/12  Added -c option (case insensitive filematching)
0000:                   
0000:                   * Need to do 1 things:
0000:                   *   Fix '*' wildcards (ex. DIR *.lzh returns completely different than
0000:                   *      DIR *lzh - 1st only does files with ONE '.' char, 2nd does mix of ONE
0000:                   *      and >1, but not all the same as first example???)
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   dir
0000:                            ttl   program module       
0000:                   
0000:                   * Disassembled 94/11/18 12:51:39 by Alan DeKok
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            endc
0000:                   
