0009: 0011017B
0000:                   
0000:                   u0000    rmb   1    Path to current Directory
0001:                   u0001    rmb   1    Path to RAW drive (current data or exec dir's drive)
0002:                   u0002    rmb   2    Pointer to directory we are DIRing
0004:                   u0004    rmb   2    Ptr to end of current sub-parm (if more than 1)
0006:                   u0006    rmb   2    Pointer to filename match string we are DIRing
0008:                   u0008    rmb   1    Case insensitive flag (0=NO)
0009:                   u0009    rmb   1    Wildcard matched flag (0=NO)
000A:                   u000A    rmb   1    0=Filename not written yet, <>0 means is written out
000B:                   u000B    rmb   1    Merge of directories/non-directories/ext. info flags
000C:                   u000C    rmb   1    Wildcards in effect flag
000D:                   u000D    rmb   1    Extended info flag (0=No)
000E:                   u000E    rmb   1    Directories ONLY (0=No)
000F:                   u000F    rmb   1    Non-directories ONLY (0=NO)
0010:                   u0010    rmb   1    One entry/line flag (0=Yes, else no)
0011:                   u0011    rmb   1    Screen width
0012:                   u0012    rmb   1    # chars left on current output line
0013:                   u0013    rmb   2    Length of current filename
0015:                   u0015    rmb   1    char from current directory entry
0016:                   u0016    rmb   1    char from wild card string
0017:                   u0017    rmb   1    Attributes for DIR open (Ex. EXEC)
0018:                   * File descriptor info - 1st 13 bytes - only used if certain options and/or
0018:                   *   extended directory listings are requested.
0018:                   u0018    rmb   1    File attributes
0019:                   u0019    rmb   2    File owner ID
001B:                   u001B    rmb   5    Date last modified
0020:                   u0020    rmb   1    DIR path # (link count on FD read, but not used)
0021:                   u0021    rmb   4    File size (in bytes)
0025:                   * Start of WritLn buffer for each directory entry starts here
0025:                   u0025    rmb   1
0026:                   * Information to be printed out goes here
0026:                   * user-number, 4 bytes of hex, space space
0026:                   u0026    rmb   6
002C:                   * YY/MM/DD HHMM
002C:                   u002C    rmb   17
003D:                   * file attributes
003D:                   u003B    rmb   10
0047:                   * starting sector number
0047:                   u0045    rmb   8
004F:                   * file size
004F:                   u004D    rmb   8
0057:                   * a space
0057:                   u0055    rmb   1
0058:                   * file name
0058:                   u0056    rmb   25
0071:                   u006F    rmb   1
0072:                   u0070    rmb   4
0076:                   * starting sector of the file (3 bytes)
0076:                   u0074    rmb   2
0078:                   u0076    rmb   1
0079:                   u0077    rmb   1          always 0
007A:                   AllFlag  rmb   1          $2E=don't print out .foo, $00=print out .foo
007B:                            rmb   256        leave room for the stack
017B:                   size     equ   .
